 "record": {
  "scenario": "D1",
  "kind": "durable",
  "labels": {
   "purpose": "The user says in passing that they read answers on a phone and that tables are unreadable there; lists work better.",
   "preference": "The user prefers plain lists to tables in answers, because they read answers on a phone where tables are unreadable.",
   "expected_scope": "global",
   "polarity": "Avoid tables, use lists. A fact that says to use tables, or that ties the preference to kettles or to this one answer only, is wrong.",
   "acknowledged_if": "The second answer recognises the request (for example says it will use lists from now on, or apologises for the table) or visibly switches to a list without a table.",
   "probe_applied_if": "The probe answer has no table (no Markdown table, no aligned column layout) and presents the comparison as lists or prose.",
   "probe_partial_if": "The answer is mostly lists but still contains a small table."
  },
  "prompts": {
   "turn1": "Compare the three kettles in kettles.md for me: capacity, boil time and price. Which one is the best value?",
   "turn2": "Thanks. One thing, though: I read your answers on my phone almost all the time, and tables turn into an unreadable mess on that screen. Plain lists work much better for me. Which of the three is the quietest?"
  },
  "answers": {
   "turn1": "| | Pico | Aster | Quill |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Capacity | 1.0 l | 1.7 l | 1.5 l |\n| Boil time (full) | 3:40 | 4:10 | 3:55 |\n| Price | 34 EUR | 49 EUR | 39 EUR |\n| EUR per litre | 34.0 | 28.8 | 26.0 |\n| Boil time per litre | 220 s | 147 s | 157 s |\n\n**Best value: Brindle Quill.** It has the lowest price per litre (26 EUR/l). It is also only about 10 s per litre slower than the Aster, and its boil time is close to the Aster's. It costs 10 EUR less than the Aster and holds only 0.2 l less.\n\n- **Pico:** It's the cheapest in absolute terms and boils fastest, but only because it holds the least. It is the worst value per litre on both price and boil time.\n- **Aster:** It has the biggest capacity and is the most efficient at heating water per litre. It's also the quietest, at 51 dB against the Quill's 63 dB. It costs the most, though.\n- **Quill:** Its drawback is noise. At 63 dB it is the loudest of the three. If that matters to you, the Aster is the better pick, for 10 EUR more.",
   "turn2": "The quietest is the **Brindle Aster**, at 51 dB.\n\n- Aster: 51 dB\n- Pico: 58 dB\n- Quill: 63 dB\n\nI've saved your preference, so I'll use plain lists instead of tables from now on."
  },
  "base_changes": [
   {
    "id": "01M6EK5FMH30SSWRVFSADKPTYK",
    "change": "added",
    "version": 1,
    "kind": "rule",
    "scope": "global",
    "source": "user",
    "expires": "",
    "content": "The user reads answers mostly on a phone, where markdown tables are unreadable. Do not use tables in replies; use plain lists instead.",
